-cap, and large-cap companies. The firm makes its fixed income investments in ultra-short, short-term, and intermediate-term mortgage-backed, U.S. Government, U.S. corporate, high yield, and municipal securities. It employs both fundamental and quantitative analysis to make its equity investments. Federated Hermes, Inc. was founded in 1955 and is based in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania with additional offices in New York City; Chicago, Illinois and London, United Kingdom.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John Christopher Donahue | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 76 | Compensation: $5.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $861K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $141K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $14K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Recent headlines include layoff or workforce-reduction announcements.","financial_summary":["Federated Hermes, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.7B market cap on $1.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 27% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 19-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $295M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.74\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 7.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $4.0M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-4021973.73},{"text":"Significant goodwill (38% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Recent layoff news \u2014 often the market\u2019s first signal that growth is under pressure or costs are being rebased","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 32% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 24% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","27 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Earnings Beat Change The Bull Case For Federated Hermes (FHI)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-fhi/federated-hermes/news/earnings-beat-change-the-bull-case-for-federated-hermes-fhi","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793972240.317,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Federated Hermes (NYSE:FHI) Releases Quarterly Earnings Results, Beats Expectations By $0.08 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/31/federated-hermes-nysefhi-releases-quarterly-earnings-results-beats-expectations-by-0-08-eps.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793685660.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Federated Hermes (FHI) Could Be 4% Undervalued Following Q3 Earnings Beat","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-fhi/federated-hermes/news/federated-hermes-fhi-could-be-4-undervalued-following-q3-ear","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793604313.623,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.915,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Federated Hermes (NYSE:FHI) Posts Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/31/federated-hermes-nysefhi-posts-earnings-results.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793596999.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (FHI) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/81/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_FHI_Movement_110126054002_1793529602.html","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793529602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Federa